  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Service Under Mingmeyang
    
    Lianhinglou first appears in the administrative ice as a logistics keeper serving Grand Auditor Mingmeyang, then leader of Aurora Stack, during the declining years of the Flipper Accord — the trade agreement binding Aurora Stack and Nightfall Shelf in mutual resource dependence. His task was managing the colony's food margins as supply contracts faltered. To this end, he made repeated unauthorized visits to the forbidden chamber of ☽'dwell Teneanemus~, a sealed Nightshelf site in the Wane Oncea tunnels, where he developed a synthesis of aurora-light channeling and pressure-depth knowledge — two traditions that Aurora orthodoxy holds to be incompatible.
    
    He taught Mingmeyang The Shell Hatch, an aurora-channeled bloom-mapping technique derived from this synthesis. The Shell Hatch extended the colony's krill-harvest range at a cost the logistics records do not advertise: each use eroded the practitioner's recent memories. Mingmeyang's subsequent deterioration — noted in contemporary accounts but attributed to overwork — correlates uncomfortably well with sustained Shell Hatch practice. Lianhinglou insists she never asked him to stop. This is not exculpatory in the way he appears to believe.
    
    ## The Bastion Apex and Forbidden Techniques
    
    Lianhinglou's expedition markers and maker's-marks remain driven into the ice at the base of the Bastion Apex, the ancient crystalline structure whose corruption and desecration are documented elsewhere in this edition. The nature of what he found there is not recorded in any source I trust. His practitioner credentials — Slide Prism, Snowdrift-numb, ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral, Mechanism Refine, Soar Helm — represent a cross-cultural technical fluency that no surface-dwelling Aurora official should possess. Several of these techniques carry permanent physical costs. Lianhinglou bears the evidence: spiral scars on his flippers consistent with extraction rather than incision, and the loss of one eye to a crystal shard. He performs the Mechanism Refine one-eyed and steady-flippered.
    
    His bracers contain fire-core fragments — a Nightshelf resource with no legitimate place in an Aurora minor official's wardrobe.
    
    ## Current Position
    
    Lianhinglou now serves Grand Auditor Qeihong, who displaced Xouhoulong to lead Aurora Stack's fragmenting governance. The administrative ice is clear that Lianhinglou assisted in this transition. The nature of that assistance is not specified, which is itself a specification. He holds the rank of beacon-keeper — a minor title — and conducts himself with the careful restraint of someone whose usefulness depends on others not examining its origins too closely.
    
    He has not been examined too closely.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
